// expect: refuse E_OccursCheck
// THE OCCURS CHECK IS REPORTED. The graph's write guard notes an infinite
// type where the bind refuses it and inference drains the note at the
// judgment boundary; the drain's report is the only way the refusal reaches
// the register. On 2026-10-12 an intermediate compiler lost every such report
// (the drain's call had become a partial application, discarded by `each`),
// and the consequence was two layers away: a polymorphic self-call whose
// first Mycroft round should have refused was judged monomorphic, and a
// recursion whose type grows with every call emitted ONE twin calling itself
// instead of refusing at the eighth instantiation. This fixture holds the
// first layer; the instantiation-depth micros hold the second.
fn f(x) = x == [x]

fn main() = if f(1) { 1 } else { 0 }
